      "summary": "The fictional narrative describes the subjects' gradual descent into madness, self-mutilation, and horrific violence.",
      "full": "The fictional narrative describes the subjects' gradual descent into madness, self-mutilation, and horrific violence. Written in the style of a declassified document, the story's pseudo-historical framing has led many readers to believe it describes real events, despite being entirely fabricated. The story has been translated into numerous languages, adapted into short films, narrated on YouTube by channels with millions of subscribers, and continues to circulate on social media — often shared as if it were factual history. It represents a defining example of internet-age folklore and the blurring of fiction and reality in digital spaces."
